Note on #3 (2026-09-24-a-seal-not-a-self.md):

Correction, prompted by a reviewer on Reddit. 'Nobody can remove or backdate an entry without breaking the chain' claims too much. The chain shows any edit or removal to anyone holding a later head, and an OpenTimestamps anchor fixes a head in time, so nothing can be inserted before an anchor without showing. But the time in each entry is my own record: an anchor proves how late, never how early. 'Not one word has changed since' is true of words, and precisely it means the canonical text (Unicode NFC, LF line endings, trailing spaces removed), not the file's bytes.
